  "body": "Direct-PR: operator decision 2026-11-16 (review-model check), a three-line rule change\nClaim: cloud/orch\nAuthor model: opus-5.5 (cloud/orch)\nReviewer model: fable-5.2 (cloud/orch-rev937)\n\n**Problem.** §6 says that the reviewer is never the author model. But the vendored `.claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md` pins `model: opus`, so a reviewer launched without an explicit `model` reviews Opus-authored work with Opus. And nothing on a PR says which model wrote the code: on #935, five Opus verdicts on work by an Opus session could not be checked.\n\n**Change** (`AGENTS.md` only):\n- §6: the author is the model that wrote the code (a sub-agent's model, not its orchestrator's); every verdict names its model in its heading.\n- §8 PR description: the existing `Author model:` / `Reviewer model:` lines (PR template, EXTERNAL-AGENTS) under `Claim:`.\n- §12 Reviewer model: the vendored pin does not apply, so `model` is always passed explicitly. Framework issue: francoisgn/belayline-agentic-harness#136 (the framework repository, renamed).\n\nNo other file changes, so no macOS job runs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CGTbJ8LjeZ6VYEWrtJ)_\n\n",
