   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, cloud/orch review sub-agent, independent of the author), verbatim:**\n\n> **REQUEST CHANGES** — head 3181dc9e\n>\n> 1. **Medium** — `docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md:106,147` and `.github/pull_request_template.md:20` still require `Author model:` (and a checklist line), not `Models:`. That leaves three formats, and external agents follow their own brief. Align them or state which line wins.\n> 2. **Medium** — `AGENTS.md:116` \"every verdict starts with `Agent: <id> (<model>)`\" contradicts the mandated first lines: `EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md:117` and `.claude/agents/adversarial-reviewer.md:10,26-28`, where `Agent :` sits outside the published markers. Say \"names\" instead, or say where the line goes.\n> 3. **Low** — `AGENTS.md:165`: the reviewer is unknown when the PR opens, and may change between rounds. Say when the line is filled. In #937's body, the reviewer id `cloud/orch review sub-agent` is not a §12 id.\n>\n> **Checked**: diff against §6, §8 and §12, and against harness ORCHESTRATION §7. `issue_claims` tests pass (21), and its regexes ignore the new line. Docs consistency is green on the head. `flow-metrics` matches verdicts per line, so it is unaffected.\n\n**Fixed in e4ee7da5:**\n1. AGENTS now uses the existing `Author model:` and `Reviewer model:` lines (same names as the template and EXTERNAL-AGENTS).\n2. The verdict names its model in its heading, as EXTERNAL-AGENTS §7 sets it.\n3. `Reviewer model:` is added once a review has run, and updated if the reviewer changes. §12 says this is the English form of the framework's line, and cites francoisgn/belayline-agentic-harness#136.\n\nThe body is updated. Delta review follows.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
